Expose Wayle's native dashboard to the external Waybar using the same mapped
hidden-bar anchor path that previously worked for external Wayle dropdowns.

A GTK popover needs an already-mapped parent surface. Instead of the separate
one-pixel Shell window, every Wayle bar whose layout has `show = false` stays
mapped but becomes transparent, empty, non-exclusive and click-through. An IPC
request is delivered to the Bar instance for the selected output, which opens
the dashboard from an anchor inside that real Wayle bar. External dropdowns
force autohide off because the input serial belongs to Waybar, not Wayle.

The dashboard user-session card is also omitted, so there are no lock, logout,
reboot, or power-off actions.

